Submission log (0022), cost: the frame's layout is first taken as a fixed signature of numbers (per layer type, flags,
view count, per view swapchain, format, array size, slice and rectangle) and compared with the last one logged; the
text is formatted only when it differs. Before, every frame formatted some ten strings under a mutex, for as long as
the session ran (the 16-line cap only stopped the Log calls). Once the 16th line is out, the call returns before the
mutex. A destroyed swapchain (the application's, the full-FOV and two-layer outputs, an output remade at a new size)
leaves the format map, so it no longer grows over a session and a reused handle is not given an old format.

